    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The CPLP",
     "texto": [
      "The **CPLP** (Comunidade dos Países de Língua Portuguesa) brings together **nine countries** that have Portuguese as an official language: Portugal, Brazil, Angola, Mozambique, Cape Verde, Guinea-Bissau, São Tomé and Príncipe, Equatorial Guinea and Timor-Leste.",
      "When we talk about the African countries where Portuguese is spoken, we say **PALOP** (African Countries with Portuguese as an Official Language)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Official language and mother tongue",
     "texto": [
      "In many of these countries Portuguese is the official language, but not the first language of the whole population. In Timor-Leste and Angola, for example, it coexists with other local languages."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
